.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_GET0_PEER_SCTS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_get0_peer_scts
.Nd get SCTs received
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft const
.Fo STACK_OF
.Fa SCT
.Fc
 *SSL_get0_peer_scts(SSL *s);
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr SSL_get0_peer_scts 3
returns the signed certificate timestamps (SCTs) that have been
received.
If this is the first time that this function has been called for a given
.Sy SSL
instance, it will examine the TLS extensions, OCSP response and the
peer's certificate for SCTs.
Future calls will return the same SCTs.
.Sh RESTRICTIONS
If no Certificate Transparency validation callback has been set (using
.Sy SSL_CTX_set_ct_validation_callback
or
.Sy SSL_set_ct_validation_callback Ns ),
this function is not guaranteed to return all of the SCTs that the peer
is capable of sending.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Xr SSL_get0_peer_scts 3
returns a list of SCTs found, or NULL if an error occurs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_ct_validation_callback 3
